---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { projects, experience, skills } from '../data/career';
---
<Layout title="Teja K G | Manufacturing Engineer, Automation & Engineering Productivity" description="Teja K G is a manufacturing and engineering productivity engineer at GE HealthCare, with experience in semiconductor equipment, medical devices, manufacturing automation, Python test automation, V&V and supplier engineering.">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow">Manufacturing Engineer · Automation · Engineering Productivity</div>
      <h1 id="hero-title">I solve manufacturing problems by combining engineering, automation and software.</h1>
      <p class="lede">I work across <strong>manufacturing engineering, productivity, automation, electronics, verification &amp; validation, and supplier engineering</strong> for complex hardware in medical devices and semiconductor equipment.</p>
      <div class="hero-proof" aria-label="Career snapshot"><span>GE HealthCare</span><span>Lam Research</span><span>Medical Devices</span><span>Semiconductor Equipment</span></div>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="experience/">View experience <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button" href="resume/">View resume</a></div>
      <p class="microcopy">Manufacturing productivity · automation · V&amp;V · supplier engineering · cross-disciplinary problem solving</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="Engineering systems schematic">
      <span class="corner c1"></span><span class="corner c2"></span><span class="scanline"></span>
      <div class="visual-status"><span class="status-dot"></span> ENGINEERING SYSTEMS / ACTIVE</div>
      <div class="schematic">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 520 380" role="img" aria-label="Engineering workflow connecting mechanical process, sensing, automation and validation">
          <defs><linearGradient id="wire" x1="0" x2="1"><stop stop-color="#78d5ff" stop-opacity=".18"/><stop offset=".5" stop-color="#78d5ff"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#a5f3d0" stop-opacity=".18"/></linearGradient></defs>
          <g fill="none" stroke="#33414e" stroke-width="1"><path d="M40 70H480M40 190H480M40 310H480"/><path d="M90 35V345M260 35V345M430 35V345"/></g>
          <g fill="#0f161d" stroke="#78d5ff" stroke-width="2"><rect x="52" y="92" width="122" height="76" rx="10"/><rect x="198" y="152" width="126" height="76" rx="10"/><rect x="346" y="88" width="122" height="76" rx="10"/><rect x="198" y="278" width="126" height="56" rx="10"/></g>
          <g fill="#f4f7fa" font-family="ui-monospace,monospace" font-size="12"><text x="72" y="122">MECHANICAL</text><text x="72" y="144" fill="#9ba8b5">PROCESS</text><text x="222" y="182">SENSING</text><text x="222" y="204" fill="#9ba8b5">IMU / TEST</text><text x="370" y="118">AUTOMATION</text><text x="370" y="140" fill="#9ba8b5">PYTHON / AI</text><text x="222" y="313">VALIDATION</text></g>
          <g fill="none" stroke="url(#wire)" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M174 130H230V190H198"/><path d="M324 190H370V126H346"/><path d="M261 228V278"/><path d="M324 306H410V164"/></g>
          <g fill="#78d5ff"><circle cx="174" cy="130" r="4"/><circle cx="198" cy="190" r="4"/><circle cx="324" cy="190" r="4"/><circle cx="346" cy="126" r="4"/><circle cx="261" cy="278" r="4"/><circle cx="410" cy="164" r="4"/></g>
          <g fill="#9ba8b5" font-family="ui-monospace,monospace" font-size="10"><text x="48" y="362">SYSTEM VIEW / 01</text><text x="398" y="362">IMPACT: MEASURED</text></g>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="visual-caption"><span><strong>ENGINEERING SYSTEMS</strong><br/>Mechanical + electronics + software</span><span>01 / 06</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="trust-strip" aria-label="Career focus">
    <div><span class="section-kicker">Focus</span><strong>Physical engineering problems</strong></div>
    <div><span class="section-kicker">Method</span><strong>Measure → automate → validate</strong></div>
    <div><span class="section-kicker">Domains</span><strong>Medical devices · semiconductor equipment</strong></div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="proof">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-kicker">Proof</div><h2 id="proof">Engineering impact, not keyword collecting.</h2></div><p>The strongest work has a measurable consequence: less cycle time, lower cost, faster validation, or a customer-critical problem retired.</p></div>
    <div class="proof-grid">
      <div class="proof"><strong>90%</strong><span>cycle-time reduction from an IMU-based manufacturing fixture</span></div>
      <div class="proof"><strong>$1M+</strong><span>annual savings from the same fixture-driven improvement</span></div>
      <div class="proof"><strong>50%</strong><span>test-cycle reduction through Python-based hardware automation</span></div>
      <div class="proof"><strong>30%</strong><span>less trial-and-error time through assembly simulation</span></div>
      <div class="proof"><strong>5%</strong><span>wet-deposition tool cycle-time improvement</span></div>
      <div class="proof"><strong>$120k/yr</strong><span>estimated saving opportunity from an AI/LLM TPI automation project</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="what">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-kicker">Capabilities</div><h2 id="what">A manufacturing engineer who crosses the boundaries.</h2></div><p>Mechanical constraints, electronics, software, manufacturing reality and validation have to agree. That intersection is where the useful work happens.</p></div>
    <div class="cap-grid">
      <div class="cap"><span class="cap-number">01</span><h3>Manufacturing Productivity</h3><p>Find bottlenecks, reduce cycle time, eliminate wasted work and turn process problems into measurable improvements.</p></div>
      <div class="cap"><span class="cap-number">02</span><h3>Manufacturing Automation</h3><p>Automate repetitive testing and engineering workflows with Python, computer vision, AI/LLM approaches and simulation.</p></div>
      <div class="cap"><span class="cap-number">03</span><h3>Product &amp; Process Engineering</h3><p>Translate product requirements into practical assembly, fixture and manufacturing solutions.</p></div>
      <div class="cap"><span class="cap-number">04</span><h3>Verification &amp; Validation</h3><p>Lead hardware validation and risk-retirement work where evidence matters as much as the design.</p></div>
      <div class="cap"><span class="cap-number">05</span><h3>Supplier Engineering</h3><p>Work with suppliers through prototypes, documentation, process transfer, V&amp;V and manufacturing readiness.</p></div>
      <div class="cap"><span class="cap-number">06</span><h3>Electronics &amp; Software</h3><p>Connect mechanical hardware with electronics, firmware, test automation and software when the problem crosses disciplines.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="work">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-kicker">Selected work</div><h2 id="work">Five engineering problems worth remembering.</h2></div><p>Each project is framed as problem → engineering action → measurable result. The tool is secondary to what changed.</p></div>
    <div class="project-grid">
      {projects.map((project, index) => <article class="project"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-index">0{index + 1}</span><span class="eyebrow">{project.tag}</span></div><h3>{project.title}</h3><p>{project.problem}</p><p class="result">{project.result}</p></article>)}
    </div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="projects/">Explore engineering work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="experience">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-kicker">Experience</div><h2 id="experience">Semiconductor equipment to medical imaging.</h2></div><p>Experience spans manufacturing engineering, productivity, supplier transitions, validation and product engineering across complex hardware.</p></div>
    <div class="timeline">
      {experience.slice(0,2).map((role, index) => <article class="role"><div class="meta"><span class="role-index">0{index + 1}</span><strong>{role.company}</strong><br />{role.period}</div><div><h3>{role.role}</h3><p>{role.summary}</p></div></article>)}
    </div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="experience/">View full experience <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="skills">
    <div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-kicker">Technical stack</div><h2 id="skills">Tools are useful. Context is the differentiator.</h2></div><p>Capabilities are grouped by engineering problem rather than turned into a meaningless proficiency scoreboard.</p></div>
    <div class="skill-grid">
      {Object.entries(skills).slice(0,4).map(([name, list]) => <div class="skill"><h3>{name}</h3><div class="pill-list">{list.map(item => <span class="pill">{item}</span>)}</div></div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="skills/">See full technical skills <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="fit">
    <div class="fit-panel"><div><div class="section-kicker">Where I fit</div><h2 id="fit">Roles where manufacturing depth and automation overlap.</h2></div><div class="fit-list"><span>Manufacturing Engineer</span><span>Manufacturing Automation Engineer</span><span>Engineering Productivity Engineer</span><span>Manufacturing Technology Engineer</span><span>Semiconductor Equipment Engineer</span><span>Medical Device Manufacturing / V&amp;V</span><span>Supplier Engineer</span><span>Product / Process Engineer</span></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="final-cta"><div class="contact"><div><div class="section-kicker">Next</div><h2>Looking for hard engineering problems.</h2></div><div><p class="lede">Manufacturing automation, engineering productivity, semiconductor equipment, medical devices, supplier engineering and technical problem solving are where this experience is most useful.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="contact/">Contact</a><a class="button" href="resume/">Resume</a></div></div></div></section>
</Layout>
